code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"xvi, 312 p. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"In this landmark book, Nobel laureate Thomas C. Schelling considers the ways in which military capabilities, real or imagined, are used as bargaining power. This edition contains a new foreword by the author where he considers the book's relevance over forty years after its first publication. Included as an afterword is the text of Professor Schelling's Nobel acceptance speech in which he reflects upon the global taboo that has emerged against nuclear weapons since Hiroshima--Publisher's description."},"tableOfContents":"The diplomacy of violence -- The art of commitment -- The manipulation of risk -- The idiom of military action -- The diplomacy of ultimate survival -- The dynamics of mutual alarm -- The dialogue of competitive armament -- Afterword: An astonishing sixty years : the legacy of Hiroshima..","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"with a new preface and afterword by Thomas C. Schelling."},"Originally published: 1966.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Military policy"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"World politics"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"U104 .S33 2008"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"355/.0335"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780300143379 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0300143370 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^2008925430"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"434611985"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990126645710203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener